window.products.push({"id":77328,"name":"Beaquicy 8318084 Washer Lid Switch Assembly - Replacement for Whirlpool Ken-more washing machine - Replaces 1018522 AP6012742 PS11745957","category":"homeandappliances","retail price":0.0,"sale price":null,"image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/719CSbbM1lL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","description":"✅ 【Ultra Durable PRODUCT】: Washer Lid Switch Assembly 8318084 is located under the control panel in the upper left corner of the washing machine and includes the green ground wire.The lid switch assembly is used to detect whether the lid of the washing machine is opened or closed. When the lid is opened, the washing machine stops rotating and stirring, which can effectively protect the safety of users. ✅ 【PRODUCT INCLUDES】:Includes 1 x 8318084 washer lid switch.If your washing machine does not start, does not stir, does not rotate, or does not drain properly, it may be because the lid switch is broken and you need to replace 8318084 Lid Switch Assembly. The switch is made from durable high quality material and well-tested by the manufacturer. ✅【90 DAYS WARRANTY】:8318084 Washer Lid Switch Assembly supports 90 days return and exchange. Our company attaches great importance to the shopping experience of each customer.Risk-free shopping, If you have any quality problem during warranty period, please contact customer service in time. We will try our best to solve the problem. Customer satisfaction is our tireless pursuit. ✅【HIGH COMPATIBILITY】:8318084 Lid Switch Assembly can replacement for Whirl-pool,Ken-more,May-tag washer.Replaces for LSQ9110PW1, LSQ9110PW2, LSQ9110PW3, LSQ9110PW4, LSQ9549PW2, LSQ9659PW2, 11015944401, 11015942401, 11015952401, 11015954401, 11015962401, 11015964401, 11016102500, 11016102501, 11016102502, 11016212500, 11016212501, 11016212502, 11016212503, 11016732500, etc. ✅ 【EASY TO INSTALL】:Please disconnect the power to the washing machine and turn off the switch before starting any maintenance. You will need a 5/16-inch nut driver for the Lid Switch Assembly 8318084 repair. First, you need to remove the rear panel on the top of the washing machine, use a nut driver to loosen the screw connecting the grounding wire, remove the old switch, and replace it with a new one.","images":["https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/719CSbbM1lL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61zNIJh6ZCL._SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61TWUez1VxL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51TIpnkrEpL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51I6jTu8yCL._AC_SL1300_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31o9GyU6jnL._AC_.jpg"],"specifications":{"brand":"Beaquicy","source_asin":"B08LNBJSND","category_path":"Home & Appliances"},"sku":"BM-77328","productType":"Home & Appliances","inventory":0,"age_group":"Adult","gender":"Unisex","source_url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B08LNBJSND","source_catalog":"Amazon Reviews 2023 product metadata","source_file":"meta_Appliances.jsonl","source_asin":"B08LNBJSND","price_pending":true,"merchant_ready":false});
